The current bug report indicates that there is a problem with the `IOUtils.skip` method not adhering to its contract as specified in the Javadoc. The Javadoc mentions that the method should only skip less than the requested number of bytes if the end of the input stream has been reached. However, the actual behavior is different, as shown in the code snippet of the `skip` method:

```java
    public static long skip(InputStream input, long numToSkip) throws IOException {
        long available = numToSkip;
        while (numToSkip > 0) {
            long skipped = input.skip(numToSkip);
            if (skipped == 0) {
                break;
            }
            numToSkip -= skipped;
        }

        return available - numToSkip;
    }
```

